									<b>Remarks:</b><br/><br/>
									    1. + Refer to Annexure-I for environmental and test conditions<br/><br/>
									    2. Refer to Annexure- I (A) to know NABL accredited scope, range and uncertainty of measurement for test parameter<br/><br/>
										G-Gravel, S-Sand, M-Silt, C-Clay, LL-Liquid Limit, PL-Plastic Limit, SL-Shrinkage Limit, NP-Non Plastic, NMC-Natural Moisture Content, UCS- Unconfined Compressive Strength,CBR- California Bearing Ratio Test<br/><br/>
										UU-Unconsolidated Undrained, C-Cohesion, ɸ-Angle of Internal Friction, Pc-Preconsolidation Pressure, Cc-Compression Index, NP-Non-Plastic, MDD- Maximum dry density, OMC- Optimum moisture content, k = coefficient of permeability<br/><br/>

									<b>Notes:-</b><br/><br/>
								    	a. The information marked with an # received from customer<br/><br/>
							        	b. ^ indicates insufficient quantity of processed sample to perform specific test<br/><br/>
							        	c. If direct shear test indicates * it represents Consolidated Undrained (CU) test, if ** then it represents Consolidated Drained (CD) test, else it is Unconsolidated Undrained (UU) test<br/><br/>
							        	d. If direct shear test indicates ### it represents Consolidated Undrained (CU) test with corrected area, if ## then it represents Consolidated Drained (CD) test with corrected area, # it represents Unconsolidated Undrained (UU) test with corrected area <br/><br/>
										e. If CBR value indicate *, it represents Unsoaked CBR else it is soaked CBR<br/><br/>
										f. If Proctor results indicate * it represents Heavy compaction, else it is Light compaction test <br/><br/>
										g. If Permeability results indicate *, it represents Constant Head Test, else it is Falling Head test <br/><br/>
										h. The results listed refer only to tested parameters and sample as received from customer<br/><br/>
										i. The balance samples if any will be discarded after 15 days from the date of issue of test certificate unless otherwise specified.<br/><br/>
										j. This document shall not be reproduced in part or full without the approval of Genstru<br/><br/>

